### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal example that shows a card (a `<div>` with some content) that rotates 180 deg around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the size, colors, or animation duration to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card {
    width:260px;          /* card width */
    height:360px;         /* card height */
    perspective:800px;    /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
    cursor:pointer;       /* hand icon on hover */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card inner wrapper (the rotating part) ---------- */
.card-inner {
    position:relative;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    transition:transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front & back faces ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.card-front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* start rotated so it's hidden */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* flip the card */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-front">
            <h2>Front Title</h2>
            <p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-back">
            <h2>Back Title</h2>
            <p>More information appears here after the flip.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | The page is centered using Flexbox. |
| **2** | `.card` sets the perspective, giving depth to the 3D rotation. |
| **3** | `.card-inner` is the element that actually rotates. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps its children in 3D space. |
| **4** | Both `.card-front` and `.card-back` are positioned absolutely on top of each other. `backface-visibility:hidden` hides the backside when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **5** | On hover, `.card-inner` rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, flipping the card. |

#### Customization tips

- **Change rotation axis**: Replace `rotateY(180deg)` with `rotateX(180deg)` for a vertical flip.
- **Add more faces**: For a 4‑sided card, add another `.card-side` with `transform: rotateY(90deg)` or `rotateY(-90deg)`.
- **Add shadows or gradients**: Use `background-image` or `box-shadow` to style the faces.
- **Add content**: Replace the placeholder text with images, icons, or any HTML you like.

Enjoy creating interactive cards!
